cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the COLM 2026 paper below.
title: >-
  Preserving Long-Tailed Expert Information in Mixture-of-Experts Tuning
abstract: >-
  Official implementation of ExpertCondenser: an auxiliary-loss-free supervised
  fine-tuning framework for sparse Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) large language
  models. Combines bias-driven sparsification with always-active gated condenser
  experts to preserve the knowledge held by long-tailed experts, outperforming
  DenseMixer and ESFT by 2.5%+ on average across mathematical reasoning and
  commonsenseQA benchmarks.
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/HectorHHZ/ExpertCondenser
url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.23036
keywords:
  - mixture-of-experts
  - moe
  - supervised-fine-tuning
  - moe-finetuning
  - expert-routing
  - load-balancing
  - long-tailed-experts
  - large-language-models
